      "t": "Слушай, это незаменимая вещь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Да, так что ты не перепутай.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Может, ещё и штаны снять?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Maybe I should take off my pants too?' Senya brings out the contrast between 'maybe' and 'else' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Ладно, спокойно работайте.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Alright, work calmly.' Fedya anchors the line on 'all right', while 'work' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Ты куда мясо дел?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Where did you put the meat?' The grammar packs 'you' and 'matters' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange. Senya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мясо лежит вот здесь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The meat is right here.' The meaning hinges on 'meat' working together with 'here' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я сделал сплошной карман.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I made a through pocket.' The grammar packs 'I' and 'pocket' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И оно падает прямо вниз.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And it falls straight down.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'and' and finishing on 'downstairs'. Fedya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Да уж, просто невероятно!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes indeed, simply unbelievable!' Notice how Russian expresses 'yes' and 'incredibly' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты ещё моё устройство не видел.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You have not seen my device yet.' Senya anchors the line on 'you', while 'saw' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это устройство для масла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is a device for oil.' Senya brings out the contrast between 'this' and 'device' in a few short words. Fedya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Ты что, бутылку к ноге привязал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did you tie a bottle to your leg?' In Russian, the idea of 'you' flows naturally into 'tied' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Слушай, это незаменимая вещь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Listen, this is an indispensable thing.' The grammar packs 'listen' and 'thing' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Да, так что ты не перепутай.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, so do not mix it up.' Fedya anchors the line on 'yes', while 'mix up' completes the thought. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
